**Done.** `router.py` now sends exchange-rate complaints to fees_fx and `NOTES.md` explains the rule.

**→ What the override does.** Any mention of an exchange, conversion, FX or currency rate becomes fees_fx. When Laya said disputes, a bare "rate" next to a complaint word, or "charged the wrong amount" for a purchase, also flips to fees_fx. When Laya said cards, a question about the cost of foreign cash flips to fees_fx. All other messages keep Laya's answer.

**→ Guarded cases.** ATM "wrong amount" complaints, pending or declined payments, double charges and refunds have no rate word, so they stay in disputes.

**→ Verification gap, important.** The sandbox blocked every Python command, so I could not run the checker. I traced all 32 evidence rows by hand and each one matches. A checker script is at `<tmp> Run it with the step directory as its one argument to confirm before the hidden test.

